# Iteration 1

## DEC-001 — Credential primitive = setup-token OAuth token via CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
- **Decision:** The portable credential artifact is the 1-year OAuth token string produced by
  `claude setup-token`, injected per-process via the `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` env var. NOT a
  keychain/`.credentials.json` transplant.
- **Rationale:** Verified on CLI v2.1.193 — setup-token prints a standalone token, writes no
  credential file, and `auth status` does not treat the slot as logged in. The token is an
  inherently portable bearer string; this dissolves the cross-platform keychain-vs-file divergence.
- **Alternatives ruled out:** keychain-item transplant; `.credentials.json` transplant; full
  interactive `auth login` per slot (browser every use). Token-env-var beats all on portability +
  browser-decoupling + cross-platform parity.
- **Context:** via /spec interview (iteration 1), OPEN #1, after Levi's isolated setup-token test.
- **Open dependency — RESOLVED:** `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=<tok> claude auth status` returns
  `loggedIn:true, authMethod:oauth_token` but **NO email**. Env-token auth works, but per-launch
  email verification via `auth status` is NOT available. → Verification (#4) shifts to mint-time
  identity capture + liveness signal. (See interview transcript; revisit in #4 ACs.)

## DEC-002 — v1 boundary = portable core, macOS-verified
- **Decision:** v1 ships N accounts, CLI tabs + SDK launch, slots = `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` + bound
  `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN`. Mechanism built platform-agnostically and **verified on macOS**.
  Linux/WSL documented as "expected to work, same mechanism, untested." Windows/PowerShell
  **explicitly deferred** to ride with the team-provisioning layer.
- **Rationale:** token-string credential dissolves the keychain-vs-file cross-platform risk, so the
  core is portable cheaply; but Levi can't verify Windows (on mac), and Windows mainly serves the
  already-deferred team layer. Verified-facts-only discipline → don't claim untested platforms.
- **Alternatives ruled out:** (a) thin 2-account mac-only proof — guts the SDK point, which is the
  objective; mac+Linux-both-verified — extra setup for marginal v1 value; full Windows now — pulls
  deferred team layer forward, unverifiable now.
- **Context:** via /spec interview (iteration 1), OPEN #9.

## DEC-003 — Architecture splits by surface: env-token (SDK) + sequential switch (interactive)
- **Decision:** Concurrency is required only for SDK/headless agents, delivered by the oat token via
  `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN` per process (PROVEN). Interactive sessions do NOT honor the env token
  (observed) and don't need concurrency — interactive uses whole-environment **sequential**
  switching. The macOS concurrent-stored-login question is therefore moot.
- **Rationale:** Empirically, `-p`/SDK runs use the env token; an interactive launch with the same
  token ran the login wizard instead. Levi confirmed sequential interactive is acceptable (his
  alias already does it).
- **Alternatives ruled out:** forcing concurrent interactive on macOS (blocked by single shared
  Keychain item; unnecessary given the steer).
- **Context:** via /spec interview (iteration 1), architecture pivot from the setup-token tests.

## DEC-005 — Capture/binding trust model = human attestation at mint, scope-forced
- **Decision:** The setup-token oat carries `user:inference` ONLY (no `user:profile`), so scripted
  email-readback is structurally impossible. v1 binds `label→email` **once at mint by human
  attestation**, made reliable by the consent page's account display ("Logged in as <email>") +
  Switch-account affordance, optionally hardened by routing the captured OAuth URL into a
  logged-out/incognito context to force deliberate account selection. The secret (oat string) is
  auto-captured from setup-token stdout; the email is **retyped + confirmed** by the human at
  capture (the tool cannot auto-read it — browser-side, and the oat lacks profile scope).
- **Rationale:** verified 2026-06-26 — two mint runs showed the consent page names the account and
  incognito enforces explicit login; token scope is inference-only. Binding is permanent because an
  oat cannot change accounts after mint. Only residual mis-bind risk = fat-fingering the email →
  mitigated by retype-confirm.
- **Alternatives ruled out:** scripted profile-endpoint readback (impossible — scope); `.claude.json`
  cache readback (impossible — token-auth never caches profile); userID fingerprint (dead —
  per-config-dir, not account-keyed). No verification spike needed.
- **Context:** via /spec interview (iteration 1), OPEN #4, after Levi's instrumented mint test.

## DEC-004 — Interactive switch mechanism = reauth (`auth login`) for v1
- **Decision:** v1 interactive switching uses the official reauth flow (`claude auth login [--email]`).
  The no-reauth credential-blob swap (swap Keychain `claudeAiOauth` + `oauthAccount`) is **deferred**
  to a future iteration (see deferred.md D-001).
- **Rationale:** reauth is robust, self-verifying (login UI shows account), survives CLI updates, and
  is trivial to build/distribute. No-reauth swap depends on undocumented Keychain/JSON internals
  Anthropic can change — unacceptable fragility for a *distributable* tool's backbone. Levi confirmed.
- **Alternatives ruled out (for v1):** no-reauth blob-swap as the default mechanism (fragile,
  spoof-prone, higher maintenance) — preserved as a deferred enhancement, not discarded.
- **Context:** via /spec interview (iteration 1).

## DEC-006 — Credential store = local per-user file, record-per-label, no sync
- **Decision:** oats live in a **per-user local file outside the repo AND outside iCloud** (e.g.
  `~/.collevity/…` or `~/.config/claude-account-switcher/`), JSON **record-per-label**
  (`{email, oat, …}` — option 3 minimal seam), `chmod 600`. The non-secret **registry**
  (label→email, settings, profile associations) is conceptually separable and may sync freely; only
  the **oat** is the protected secret. v1 does NOT sync the secret. The store-backend abstraction
  (for 1Password/`op`) is **deferred** ("not there yet"). Encryption-at-rest is **deferred** —
  FileVault + `600` perms is the v1 at-rest posture.
- **Rationale:** portability (mac + Linux identical — upholds DEC-002), simplicity, zero runtime
  deps, and the secret never touches a versioned or synced tree. `.gitignore` does NOT stop iCloud
  sync (independent mechanisms) → safety comes from *physical location*, not ignore rules. iCloud
  multi-device sync of the secret rejected for v1: plaintext bearer token on Apple's cloud + every
  synced device, and a bad default for a *distributable* tool (would stash Levi's account token in an
  employee's iCloud). Reconsiderable later only WITH encryption-at-rest (see D-003). Mitigating
  factor: oats are Levi's own accounts, inference-scoped, fast to revoke + re-mint.
- **Alternatives ruled out:** macOS Keychain (mac-only — breaks portability; clunky record/metadata
  story); 1Password/`op` now (heavy dependency in every SDK launch path — reserved as the team-layer
  backend behind a future abstraction); iCloud-synced plaintext secret (blast radius + unsafe
  default); building the store-backend abstraction now (deferred, avoid unused machinery).
- **Context:** via /spec interview (iteration 1), STORE axis. Levi: "I'm fine with local for now."

## DEC-007 — Command surface = surface-split verbs, runner (not env-export) for SDK
- **Decision:** CLI named **`claude-switch`** (canonical, for written/non-coder direction) + **`cas`**
  (symlink alias). Verbs:
  - `add <label>` — guided mint (logged-out browser), **retype-confirm email**, liveness-check the
    fresh oat, store record + create the slot's config dir. Label **defaults to the email local-part**
    (fs-safe), user override allowed; labels must be **unique** (= store key AND config-dir name;
    collision forces a custom label).
  - `list` — slots: label, email, oat age/health, and which account is the **active interactive
    login** (matched via `auth status` email → label).
  - `run <label> -- <cmd…>` — SDK/headless: launch the child with `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=<slot>` +
    `CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=<oat>` injected **for that process only** (runner pattern). Concurrency
    deliverable; echoes "running as `<label>` (`<email>`)".
  - `use <label>` — interactive: sequential whole-env switch via `claude auth login --email` (DEC-004).
  - `rm <label>` — drop from store + guide server-side revoke (single-scope `user:inference` rule).
- **Rationale:** the surface splits along the architecture — SDK is a per-process **runner** that
  never mutates the shell (satisfies the zero-shell-disruption non-negotiable and makes concurrency
  collision-free); interactive is a sequential global switch. Runner beats env-printer on token
  hygiene: the oat's lifetime = the child process, never entering shell env/history, no manual unset,
  no cross-slot race. Each slot = per-label config dir (`~/.collevity/slots/<label>/`) + bound oat.
- **Alternatives ruled out:** env-printer (`eval "$(cas env <label>)"`) as the default — leaks the
  year-long oat into the shell env + history, needs manual `unset`, races across slots (preserved as
  a possible power-user `env` extra, deferred); a single verb spanning both surfaces (conflates
  concurrent-vs-sequential semantics).
- **Context:** via /spec interview (iteration 1), slot/command-surface axis.
